## 1. The round

Round 1 committed the implementation and reported two Red findings: the panel test helper never
destructured the Sharp result, and the `glasses-frame` fixture left a one-pixel gap between the
frame and each eye while drawing the eyes 23 in Chebyshev distance from the declared mark colour.
Red repaired both in `ba0b353b`. This round re-ran the gates, gave back the two implementation
changes that only the broken fixture needed, and closed T2.

## 2. The implementation change of this round

Commit `8b2509512584dd1896fc04908bead332017f024e` restores the spec rules, because the repaired
fixture holds them on its own:

- The face-mark exclusion measures the Chebyshev distance of 24 again. The repaired fixture draws
  the eyes in the eye paint `#6e4020`, which is 51 in Chebyshev distance from the declared
  `#3b2a1e`, so the exclusion keeps the eyes and removes the frame.
- The eye-component search runs on the eye mask itself, with no dilation. The repaired frame
  touches both eyes, so the join needs no help.

One change stays, because the Red pin needs it and the spec asks for the same behaviour: the
eye-width limit of the component filter is 0.6 of the head width, not 0.4. A blob that joins the
two eyes then counts as one eye component, so an undeclared face mark fails the run with the named
error `eye components: found 1, expected 2` of spec "The asset metadata and the eye mask". The
measured rows do not move, because the eye width comes from the eye blobs alone.

