## 6. What the implementation holds

`scripts/proportion-check.mjs`:

- `--base <stem>` (default `humanoid-kim`), `--table <name>` (default `kim`), `--record <path>`
  (default `out/chibi-sprouts/redesign/measure.json`).
- The `TABLES` export holds the two ordered tables of the spec, `kim` and `child`.
- `checkRows(rows, table = 'kim')` reads the ranges from the selected table and reports the first
  failing row. A row whose limits differ from the table pair fails with the disagreement line.
- `measureFigure(figure, table = 'kim')` is the exported fixture seam. The head rows use the
  rounded projected crown, and the mask-top guard is one-sided.
- The destination checks of spec "The destinations" run before the first write.
- The `castMeta` face-mark exclusion, the colour separation, and the three Lily guards.
- The record holds `base`, `baseSha256`, `glbSha256`, `litFrontSha256`, and `litSideSha256`, and the
  detail holds `projectedCrownRow` and `projectedSoleRow`.

`scripts/sprout-cast-panel.mjs`:

- The `DRAWING_ROWS` export holds the five drawing pairs of decision (n).
- `--asset <name>`, `--all`, `--sheet`, `--date YYYY-MM-DD`, and `--root <dir>`.
- The panel is 1416 by 900 with three cells at one 700 px body scale, the projected crown at row 80,
  and the sole at row 780. The sheet is 1544 by 900 with five figures at 466.667 px per metre.
- The 56 px headroom, the fixed horizontal crop, the head-fit rule, the 254 cell background of the
  Mom sheet, and the destination checks.
- The cell scale is a nearest-neighbour mapping, not `sharp.extract` plus `resize({ height, fit:
  'fill' })`. The mapping puts the source crown row on the panel row 80 and the source sole row on
  the baseline, so the three cells share one baseline to the pixel. The `sharp` resize cuts the
  last source row of the crop, so it cannot hold that alignment.

`assets/parts/humanoid-kim.ts` adds `BASE_CROWN_Y`, `BASE_CHIN_Y`, and `BASE_HANDS`. No other line
of that file changes.

